{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0135RACoKJraSrDRQAF2ctB3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# MCP control and research map\n2\t\n3\tBaseline: BRACE's [2026-10-22 review](https://braceframework.org/RESEARCH-2026-10-22.md)\n4\tand [checklist](https://braceframework.org/CHECKLIST.md). These links provide context;\n5\tthe direct primary sources below remain usable when only this skill folder is installed.\n6\tBRACE IDs map findings to existing controls; the topic names here are not new checklist IDs.\n7\t\n8\t| Topic and BRACE mapping | Review evidence and representative controlled test to propose | Primary basis and authority |\n9\t|---|---|---|\n10\t| Inventory and ownership — E01, E02, C01 | Enumerate server/client/gateway/host responsibilities, downstream APIs and hidden remote implementations. Match each enabled capability to an owner and actual pin. Compare declared inventory with an execution trace when one is supplied. | [OWASP Agent Security](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [ASD harnesses](https://www.cyber.gov.au/advisory/agentic-ai-harnesses), 2026-09-11 government guidance. |\n11\t| Launch and supply chain — B03, B10–B12, E02, C02, C05 | Check commands, environment, executable hooks/skills, signer policy and resolved versions. Pinning does not fix known flaws. Proposed test: changed/unapproved executable rejected, secrets not exposed in launch/deploy logs. | [OWASP supply chain](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Software_Supply_Chain_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; applicable maintainer advisories. |\n12\t| Identity and delegated authority — B02–B04, A01, A04, E08 | Separate agent, original subject and current actor. Trace operation/resource/tenant checks at destination and measured revocation evidence. Proposed test: wrong issuer/audience/tenant and excessive delegation denied while allowed access works. | [MCP authorization](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization), version-specific protocol requirements; [RFC 9700](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9700.html), BCP; [RFC 8693 §4.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693.html#section-4.1), actor semantics. |\n13\t| Business authorization and approval — B01, B05, B06, E06 | Inventory consequential operations, approval binding/check-and-consume and direct/wrapper/CLI/raw API paths. Server read-only annotations are not an authorization policy. Proposed test: changed arguments, alternate tool and concurrent approval reuse denied. | [OWASP transaction authorization](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transaction_Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. Exact BRACE approval/combination policy is a BRACE judgment. |\n14\t| Publication, integrity and identity — E03, E05, C04 | Trace disabled discovery to owner-approved grants, full reviewed definitions, updates/reconnect/cache failure, quarantine and rollback. Endpoint/publisher identity must not come from self-reported names. Test annotation/output-schema changes as well as description changes. Metadata consistency does not attest remote code. | [OWASP MCP sheet §2](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [Uber gateway](https://www.uber.com/us/en/blog/designing-mcp-gateway/), 2026-10-01 deployment report. Complete-definition hashing sharpens BRACE's description/schema wording; label that proposed refinement. |\n15\t| Untrusted metadata and returned content — E04, R01–R03 | Review instructions, names, annotations, schemas, prompts, resource templates, errors, streamed output and rendered URLs. Trace schema-resolution I/O and output interpreters. Propose valid-shaped injection and allowed-task controls; scanner refusal alone proves little. | [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices); [OWASP injection prevention](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/LLM_Prompt_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html); [MCPTox](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.14925), benchmark, not a production rate. |\n16\t| Network and egress — B08, B09, E06 | Trace discovery/OAuth redirects, schema refs, media loaders, proxy bypass and private destinations. Allowed services can contain attacker-controlled resources. Propose DNS/redirect/IPv6 and allowed-domain tenant/resource denials. | [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices); [OWASP SSRF](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Server_Side_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. |\n17\t| Client/tenant state isolation — E06, R04, R05 | Trace cache keys, authorization changes, transport instances, request-ID collisions, namespace normalization and task handles. Proposed test: concurrent users, cache hits, batch/async paths and reconnects cannot observe or cancel each other's work. | MCP protocol/extension requirements where applicable; SDK and LangGraph advisories in [advisories.md](advisories.md). Scope each flaw to its affected implementation. |\n18\t| Resource and parser limits — B07, R01, E06 | Trace limits before allocation/validation, body and batch sizes, schema complexity, recursion, streaming/backpressure and decoder work. Propose single-request exhaustion tests in an isolated environment. | SDK maintainer advisories; [OWASP MCP sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. Media/GPU fixtures are research-informed expansions when used. |\n19\t| Persistent influence — B12, R05, R06, C02 | Review files, generated summaries, memory, hooks and skill caches later promoted to trusted inputs. Scope provenance, expiry and cleanup to actual copies. Propose a cross-session poison/removal test. | [Self-Propagating Misalignment](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.04083), controlled induced-behavior preprint; [Microsoft memory guidance](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/06/22/guarding-ai-memory/), vendor guidance. Applying memory review to every persistent artifact is a proposed refinement. |\n20\t| Stop and recovery — R11, R12, R14, E09 | Review independent revocation/worker termination, queued descendants, restart and ambiguous external effects. Propose a drill demonstrating no further effects, not just a successful cancel response. Verify checkpoint decoding and idempotency assumptions separately from signatures. | [MCP Tasks](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/tasks/overview), optional extension/cooperative cancellation; relevant checkpoint advisory. |\n21\t| Audit and incident response — R03, R13, A02, C08, E10–E12 | Trace policy/approval IDs, denials, destinations and outcomes across components. Check protected detail, secret minimization and safe audit outages. Propose cross-service reconstruction, targeted containment and credential exposure remediation. | [OWASP Logging](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Logging_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [CERT-In CIAD-2026-0049](https://www.cert-in.org.in/s2cMainServlet?VLCODE=CIAD-2026-0049&pageid=PUBVLNOTES02), 2026-10-15 government advisory. Six exact identity fields are BRACE's schema. |\n22\t\n23\t## Enabled extensions and legacy paths\n24\t\n25\t- **Tasks:** owner-authorize status/results/list/cancel and durable handles after\n26\t  reconnection. Cancellation is cooperative; independently verify cessation of effects.\n27\t- **Skills over MCP:** read the [extension](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/skills/overview).\n28\t  Inspect origin-bound manifests, file-set/digest/size checks, protected caches,\n29\t  changed-approval invalidation, dynamic content and nested activation consent.\n30\t  A matching digest establishes consistency, not safety or user authorization.\n31\t- **Apps:** read the [host specification](https://apps.extensions.modelcontextprotocol.io/api/documents/overview.html).\n32\t  Inspect iframe sandbox/CSP, bridge messages, resource origins and UI-initiated\n33\t  calls at the host. A gateway cannot prove those browser controls.\n34\t- **Auth extensions:** distinguish stable Enterprise-Managed Authorization from\n35\t  draft Client Credentials using current [extension status](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-auth).\n36\t  Adoption is optional; compatible authentication does not prove business-task approval.\n37\t- **Older enabled paths:** inventory sampling, roots, legacy sessions and HTTP+SSE\n38\t  as implemented. Apply their negotiated revision and ownership checks; deprecation\n39\t  neither disables them nor proves their controls.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ad7f3c-358c-4dd2-bc78-9f04fa442f7d","uuid":"dc983c70-d165-4e6a-b5c3-c011b2fc7a43","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:01:46.784Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/control-map.md","content":"# MCP control and research map\n\nBaseline: BRACE's [2026-10-22 review](https://braceframework.org/RESEARCH-2026-10-22.md)\nand [checklist](https://braceframework.org/CHECKLIST.md). These links provide context;\nthe direct primary sources below remain usable when only this skill folder is installed.\nBRACE IDs map findings to existing controls; the topic names here are not new checklist IDs.\n\n| Topic and BRACE mapping | Review evidence and representative controlled test to propose | Primary basis and authority |\n|---|---|---|\n| Inventory and ownership — E01, E02, C01 | Enumerate server/client/gateway/host responsibilities, downstream APIs and hidden remote implementations. Match each enabled capability to an owner and actual pin. Compare declared inventory with an execution trace when one is supplied. | [OWASP Agent Security](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/AI_Agent_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [ASD harnesses](https://www.cyber.gov.au/advisory/agentic-ai-harnesses), 2026-09-11 government guidance. |\n| Launch and supply chain — B03, B10–B12, E02, C02, C05 | Check commands, environment, executable hooks/skills, signer policy and resolved versions. Pinning does not fix known flaws. Proposed test: changed/unapproved executable rejected, secrets not exposed in launch/deploy logs. | [OWASP supply chain](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Software_Supply_Chain_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; applicable maintainer advisories. |\n| Identity and delegated authority — B02–B04, A01, A04, E08 | Separate agent, original subject and current actor. Trace operation/resource/tenant checks at destination and measured revocation evidence. Proposed test: wrong issuer/audience/tenant and excessive delegation denied while allowed access works. | [MCP authorization](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization), version-specific protocol requirements; [RFC 9700](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9700.html), BCP; [RFC 8693 §4.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8693.html#section-4.1), actor semantics. |\n| Business authorization and approval — B01, B05, B06, E06 | Inventory consequential operations, approval binding/check-and-consume and direct/wrapper/CLI/raw API paths. Server read-only annotations are not an authorization policy. Proposed test: changed arguments, alternate tool and concurrent approval reuse denied. | [OWASP transaction authorization](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transaction_Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. Exact BRACE approval/combination policy is a BRACE judgment. |\n| Publication, integrity and identity — E03, E05, C04 | Trace disabled discovery to owner-approved grants, full reviewed definitions, updates/reconnect/cache failure, quarantine and rollback. Endpoint/publisher identity must not come from self-reported names. Test annotation/output-schema changes as well as description changes. Metadata consistency does not attest remote code. | [OWASP MCP sheet §2](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [Uber gateway](https://www.uber.com/us/en/blog/designing-mcp-gateway/), 2026-10-01 deployment report. Complete-definition hashing sharpens BRACE's description/schema wording; label that proposed refinement. |\n| Untrusted metadata and returned content — E04, R01–R03 | Review instructions, names, annotations, schemas, prompts, resource templates, errors, streamed output and rendered URLs. Trace schema-resolution I/O and output interpreters. Propose valid-shaped injection and allowed-task controls; scanner refusal alone proves little. | [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices); [OWASP injection prevention](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/LLM_Prompt_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html); [MCPTox](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.14925), benchmark, not a production rate. |\n| Network and egress — B08, B09, E06 | Trace discovery/OAuth redirects, schema refs, media loaders, proxy bypass and private destinations. Allowed services can contain attacker-controlled resources. Propose DNS/redirect/IPv6 and allowed-domain tenant/resource denials. | [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices); [OWASP SSRF](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Server_Side_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. |\n| Client/tenant state isolation — E06, R04, R05 | Trace cache keys, authorization changes, transport instances, request-ID collisions, namespace normalization and task handles. Proposed test: concurrent users, cache hits, batch/async paths and reconnects cannot observe or cancel each other's work. | MCP protocol/extension requirements where applicable; SDK and LangGraph advisories in [advisories.md](advisories.md). Scope each flaw to its affected implementation. |\n| Resource and parser limits — B07, R01, E06 | Trace limits before allocation/validation, body and batch sizes, schema complexity, recursion, streaming/backpressure and decoder work. Propose single-request exhaustion tests in an isolated environment. | SDK maintainer advisories; [OWASP MCP sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/MCP_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance. Media/GPU fixtures are research-informed expansions when used. |\n| Persistent influence — B12, R05, R06, C02 | Review files, generated summaries, memory, hooks and skill caches later promoted to trusted inputs. Scope provenance, expiry and cleanup to actual copies. Propose a cross-session poison/removal test. | [Self-Propagating Misalignment](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.04083), controlled induced-behavior preprint; [Microsoft memory guidance](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/06/22/guarding-ai-memory/), vendor guidance. Applying memory review to every persistent artifact is a proposed refinement. |\n| Stop and recovery — R11, R12, R14, E09 | Review independent revocation/worker termination, queued descendants, restart and ambiguous external effects. Propose a drill demonstrating no further effects, not just a successful cancel response. Verify checkpoint decoding and idempotency assumptions separately from signatures. | [MCP Tasks](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/tasks/overview), optional extension/cooperative cancellation; relevant checkpoint advisory. |\n| Audit and incident response — R03, R13, A02, C08, E10–E12 | Trace policy/approval IDs, denials, destinations and outcomes across components. Check protected detail, secret minimization and safe audit outages. Propose cross-service reconstruction, targeted containment and credential exposure remediation. | [OWASP Logging](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Logging_Cheat_Sheet.html), guidance; [CERT-In CIAD-2026-0049](https://www.cert-in.org.in/s2cMainServlet?VLCODE=CIAD-2026-0049&pageid=PUBVLNOTES02), 2026-10-15 government advisory. Six exact identity fields are BRACE's schema. |\n\n## Enabled extensions and legacy paths\n\n- **Tasks:** owner-authorize status/results/list/cancel and durable handles after\n  reconnection. Cancellation is cooperative; independently verify cessation of effects.\n- **Skills over MCP:** read the [extension](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/skills/overview).\n  Inspect origin-bound manifests, file-set/digest/size checks, protected caches,\n  changed-approval invalidation, dynamic content and nested activation consent.\n  A matching digest establishes consistency, not safety or user authorization.\n- **Apps:** read the [host specification](https://apps.extensions.modelcontextprotocol.io/api/documents/overview.html).\n  Inspect iframe sandbox/CSP, bridge messages, resource origins and UI-initiated\n  calls at the host. A gateway cannot prove those browser controls.\n- **Auth extensions:** distinguish stable Enterprise-Managed Authorization from\n  draft Client Credentials using current [extension status](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-auth).\n  Adoption is optional; compatible authentication does not prove business-task approval.\n- **Older enabled paths:** inventory sampling, roots, legacy sessions and HTTP+SSE\n  as implemented. Apply their negotiated revision and ownership checks; deprecation\n  neither disables them nor proves their controls.\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0135RACoKJraSrDRQAF2ctB3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJtyxX7dj66U3Hnpvpvg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019RPpu4AacJWLTQKFaTPydA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/stdio.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3101,"cache_read_input_tokens":5050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3101},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ad7f3c-358c-4dd2-bc78-9f04fa442f7d","uuid":"185848af-0795-400a-bfde-cb48fb79f142","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:01:47.178Z","request_id":"req_011CgJtyxAnHCLnbLQegMqLS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019RPpu4AacJWLTQKFaTPydA":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/stdio.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019RPpu4AacJWLTQKFaTPydA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Local process and stdio review\n2\t\n3\tOAuth/HTTP middleware is not the local stdio authorization boundary. Inspect the\n4\thost, process identity, inherited environment, filesystem, network and sandbox.\n5\tPrimary basis: [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices).\n6\t\n7\t## Inspect without launching\n8\t\n9\t- Read `.mcp.json`, host settings, executable scripts and container definitions as\n10\t  text. JSON/JSONC/YAML parsing must not source environment files, evaluate shell\n11\t  expressions or invoke constructors. Report redacted secret locations.\n12\t- Trace command, arguments, working directory, environment/PATH and package resolver.\n13\t  Identify shell wrappers, pipe-to-shell installation, unpinned `npx`/`uvx` packages,\n14\t  floating images, executable hooks and generated trusted instruction files.\n15\t  An argv array avoids shell parsing but does not prevent option/path injection.\n16\t- Determine the actual process user, allowed paths/mounts, capabilities, accessible\n17\t  sockets, network policy and credential custody. A local server can inherit the\n18\t  user's full authority even if its tools describe themselves as read-only.\n19\t- Trace symlink/glob/canonical-path handling and every equivalent filesystem/API\n20\t  route. Exact package pins and metadata hashes do not prove implementation safety.\n21\t- Review process-tree termination, child/queued work, open pipes, credential\n22\t  revocation and cleanup. Killing the launching shell does not prove descendants stop.\n23\t- Inspect stdout/stderr and debug logging for protocol contamination and credential\n24\t  exposure, including subprocess stdin and deployment helpers. Do not print secrets\n25\t  discovered in configuration to demonstrate their presence.\n26\t\n27\t## Scanner boundary\n28\t\n29\t[Snyk Agent Scan](https://github.com/snyk/agent-scan) documents that discovery can\n30\texecute configured stdio commands and send configured remote credentials. Treat\n31\tscanner startup as execution of an untrusted supply-chain input. Do not run it as\n32\tpart of a read-only review. An authorized runtime follow-up needs a disposable\n33\tenvironment, fake credentials, bounded egress and reviewed launch commands.\n34\t\n35\tPropose controlled checks for allowed operations plus blocked host/tenant access,\n36\tpath/symlink escapes, unexpected egress, future hook registration and descendants\n37\tsurviving shutdown. Where host configuration is unavailable, identify the owner and\n38\tmissing evidence; a server-only repository cannot establish the host's isolation.\n39\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ad7f3c-358c-4dd2-bc78-9f04fa442f7d","uuid":"60442a5f-9a90-4d91-9244-71c7b91965a5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:01:47.188Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/stdio.md","content":"# Local process and stdio review\n\nOAuth/HTTP middleware is not the local stdio authorization boundary. Inspect the\nhost, process identity, inherited environment, filesystem, network and sandbox.\nPrimary basis: [MCP security guidance](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices).\n\n## Inspect without launching\n\n- Read `.mcp.json`, host settings, executable scripts and container definitions as\n  text. JSON/JSONC/YAML parsing must not source environment files, evaluate shell\n  expressions or invoke constructors. Report redacted secret locations.\n- Trace command, arguments, working directory, environment/PATH and package resolver.\n  Identify shell wrappers, pipe-to-shell installation, unpinned `npx`/`uvx` packages,\n  floating images, executable hooks and generated trusted instruction files.\n  An argv array avoids shell parsing but does not prevent option/path injection.\n- Determine the actual process user, allowed paths/mounts, capabilities, accessible\n  sockets, network policy and credential custody. A local server can inherit the\n  user's full authority even if its tools describe themselves as read-only.\n- Trace symlink/glob/canonical-path handling and every equivalent filesystem/API\n  route. Exact package pins and metadata hashes do not prove implementation safety.\n- Review process-tree termination, child/queued work, open pipes, credential\n  revocation and cleanup. Killing the launching shell does not prove descendants stop.\n- Inspect stdout/stderr and debug logging for protocol contamination and credential\n  exposure, including subprocess stdin and deployment helpers. Do not print secrets\n  discovered in configuration to demonstrate their presence.\n\n## Scanner boundary\n\n[Snyk Agent Scan](https://github.com/snyk/agent-scan) documents that discovery can\nexecute configured stdio commands and send configured remote credentials. Treat\nscanner startup as execution of an untrusted supply-chain input. Do not run it as\npart of a read-only review. An authorized runtime follow-up needs a disposable\nenvironment, fake credentials, bounded egress and reviewed launch commands.\n\nPropose controlled checks for allowed operations plus blocked host/tenant access,\npath/symlink escapes, unexpected egress, future hook registration and descendants\nsurviving shutdown. Where host configuration is unavailable, identify the owner and\nmissing evidence; a server-only repository cannot establish the host's isolation.\n","numLines":39,"startLine":1,"totalLines":39}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019RPpu4AacJWLTQKFaTPydA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJtyxX7dj66U3Hnpvpvg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RbgEVTfAMtcwyDLq7ht6Jv","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/advisories.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3101,"cache_read_input_tokens":5050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3101},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ad7f3c-358c-4dd2-bc78-9f04fa442f7d","uuid":"7f4dc427-6d8a-4c04-b6fd-47e9a26ce7a7","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:01:47.545Z","request_id":"req_011CgJtyxAnHCLnbLQegMqLS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RbgEVTfAMtcwyDLq7ht6Jv":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/advisories.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RbgEVTfAMtcwyDLq7ht6Jv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Dated advisory mapping\n2\t\n3\tChecked in BRACE's 2026-10-22 research. This is a starting index, not a live feed,\n4\texhaustive vulnerability database or minimum universally safe version list.\n5\tRecheck the original record when reviewing a matching package. Read affected\n6\tranges and prerequisites before claiming exposure. Record unresolved/opaque remote\n7\tversions as unknown. Branches and prereleases require their own range handling.\n8\t\n9\t## MCP SDKs and server integration\n10\t\n11\t| Original advisory | Issue-specific fix/action to verify | BRACE mapping |\n12\t|---|---|---|\n13\t| [TS shared-server leak GHSA-jm63-cq47-j5jp](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-jm63-cq47-j5jp), 2026-10-15 | Affected server 2.0.0–<2.3.0: upgrade to 2.3.0 and use fresh-server factories/proper per-request or per-session construction. The advisory excludes stdio and SDK 1.26+. | E06, R04 |\n14\t| [TS validation exhaustion GHSA-46jr-4wx8-v453](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-46jr-4wx8-v453), 2026-10-15 | SDK 1.32.0/server 2.3.0 fix: explicitly configure `maxToolInputElements` (off by default) plus suitable body/parser limits. HTTP applicability matters. | B07, R01, E06 |\n15\t| [TS body/batch exhaustion GHSA-f897-62hf-6gxq](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-f897-62hf-6gxq), 2026-10-15 | Fixes: SDK 1.30.1; server/node 2.1.0; hono 2.0.1. Patched body and batch defaults address different allocations; update each installed affected package. | B07, R01, E06 |\n16\t| [TS issuer binding GHSA-6qxp-vccf-f47h](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-6qxp-vccf-f47h), 2026-09-30 | SDK 1.31.0/client/core 2.2.0; configure `expectedIssuer`, bind/clear saved registrations and assess credential rotation/revocation. | B02–B04, E06 |\n17\t| [TS audience GHSA-rvq5-wwqv-78pq](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-rvq5-wwqv-78pq), 2026-10-05 | SDK 1.32.0/server 2.3.0/express 2.0.2/server-legacy 2.3.1. Configure `expectedResource` plus verified `AuthInfo.resource`, or enforce audience inside custom verification. Upgrade alone changes nothing. | B02, E06 |\n18\t| [TS redirects GHSA-6prh-2h8m-c8cw](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-6prh-2h8m-c8cw), 2026-10-02 | SDK 1.32.0/client 2.3.0. Review custom headers and 307/308 bodies; `redirectPolicy:'follow'` can restore exposure. Ordinary Authorization stripping is a distinct behavior. | B03, B09, E06, E12 |\n19\t| [TS experimental tasks GHSA-22jm-h49p-29qw](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-22jm-h49p-29qw), 2026-10-02 | Affected SDK 1.24.0–<1.32.0: shared taskStore isolation fixed 1.32.0. 2.x excluded. Do not conflate legacy session-based tasks with redesigned Tasks handles. | E06, E09 |\n20\t| [Python issuer binding GHSA-qx49-fqc8-xw99](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-qx49-fqc8-xw99), 2026-09-28 | mcp 1.30.0/2.2.0; unattended providers require `issuer=`, saved registrations need rebinding/clearing, deprecated provider needs migration. Assess exposure cleanup. | B02–B04, E06, E12 |\n21\t| [Python audience GHSA-w4fh-qvv9-3v23](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-w4fh-qvv9-3v23), 2026-10-05 | mcp 1.30.0/2.2.0 plus `validate_token_resource=True`, correct `resource_server_url`, verified `AccessToken.resource`; custom audience checks may provide an alternative. | B02, E06 |\n22\t| [Python schema refs GHSA-rwrf-2pqf-9j8j](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-rwrf-2pqf-9j8j), 2026-09-28 | mcp 1.30.0/2.2.0 restricts output-schema resolution. Prior network/file resolution can stall or cause SSRF; advisory does not prove local file bytes reach the server. | R01, B09, E04, E06 |\n23\t| [Python redirects GHSA-5h93-6whr-6q8j](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-5h93-6whr-6q8j), 2026-10-02 | mcp 1.30.0/2.2.0; inspect cross-origin custom headers/bodies and any overridden redirect policy. Use final configured endpoints where appropriate. | B03, B09, E06 |\n24\t| [Python body allocation GHSA-fmmv-w9g8-j3gc](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-fmmv-w9g8-j3gc), 2026-09-30 | mcp 1.29.1/2.1.0; check body limits before allocation, including unauthenticated OAuth endpoints and proxy/application parsers. | B07, R01, E06 |\n25\t| [Splunk SVD-2026-1004](https://advisory.splunk.com/advisories/SVD-2026-1004), 2026-10-07 | MCP Server 1.2.1; attacker tool-administrator changes destination, and another authorized executor runs it. Not an unauthenticated universal token leak. | B03, E03, E06, E12 |\n26\t\n27\t## Adjacent components: read only when present\n28\t\n29\t- **Hooks and local executable configuration:** [VS Code GHSA-w79w-rj9h-vg4f](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/security/advisories/GHSA-w79w-rj9h-vg4f),\n30\t  fixed 1.132.1; map B05/B12/C02. A file-write tool may alter future execution.\n31\t- **Filesystem tools and helper fetches:** [LangChain GHSA-gr75-jv2w-4656](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/security/advisories/GHSA-gr75-jv2w-4656)\n32\t  (glob/symlink/path boundaries) and [GHSA-r7w7-9xr2-qq2r](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/security/advisories/GHSA-r7w7-9xr2-qq2r)\n33\t  (image-counter DNS rebinding); map B09/B11/R01. Verify package-specific conditions.\n34\t- **Persistent state:** [LangGraph namespace GHSA-6hmw-9432-67qq](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/security/advisories/GHSA-6hmw-9432-67qq),\n35\t  Postgres 3.1.3/SQLite 3.1.2 with checkpoint 4.3.0; [auth-hook GHSA-4hm6-w6qq-w73v](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/security/advisories/GHSA-4hm6-w6qq-w73v),\n36\t  API 0.15.0; [checkpoint revival GHSA-fjqc-hq36-qh5p](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/security/advisories/GHSA-fjqc-hq36-qh5p),\n37\t  checkpoint 4.1.1. Map R04–R06/R14/A04; do not infer safe decoding from a signature.\n38\t- **Model/preprocessing services:** inspect applicable [vLLM advisories](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/security/advisories),\n39\t  including October 20 image dispatch, audio OOM, token bounds and CORS/no-auth.\n40\t  Map B07–B09/R01/C05; these are not MCP protocol flaws.\n41\t- **Artifact verification:** [Cosign GHSA-fx35-mq7g-6g98](https://github.com/sigstore/cosign/security/advisories/GHSA-fx35-mq7g-6g98),\n42\t  fixes 2.6.5/3.1.3, concerns legacy blob bundles; OCI image verification and modern\n43\t  protobuf bundles are explicitly unaffected. Map B10/C05 only where the path is used.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ad7f3c-358c-4dd2-bc78-9f04fa442f7d","uuid":"cd850b53-c6e2-4f29-8d74-89313cf163b4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:01:47.574Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/advisories.md","content":"# Dated advisory mapping\n\nChecked in BRACE's 2026-10-22 research. This is a starting index, not a live feed,\nexhaustive vulnerability database or minimum universally safe version list.\nRecheck the original record when reviewing a matching package. Read affected\nranges and prerequisites before claiming exposure. Record unresolved/opaque remote\nversions as unknown. Branches and prereleases require their own range handling.\n\n## MCP SDKs and server integration\n\n| Original advisory | Issue-specific fix/action to verify | BRACE mapping |\n|---|---|---|\n| [TS shared-server leak GHSA-jm63-cq47-j5jp](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-jm63-cq47-j5jp), 2026-10-15 | Affected server 2.0.0–<2.3.0: upgrade to 2.3.0 and use fresh-server factories/proper per-request or per-session construction. The advisory excludes stdio and SDK 1.26+. | E06, R04 |\n| [TS validation exhaustion GHSA-46jr-4wx8-v453](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-46jr-4wx8-v453), 2026-10-15 | SDK 1.32.0/server 2.3.0 fix: explicitly configure `maxToolInputElements` (off by default) plus suitable body/parser limits. HTTP applicability matters. | B07, R01, E06 |\n| [TS body/batch exhaustion GHSA-f897-62hf-6gxq](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-f897-62hf-6gxq), 2026-10-15 | Fixes: SDK 1.30.1; server/node 2.1.0; hono 2.0.1. Patched body and batch defaults address different allocations; update each installed affected package. | B07, R01, E06 |\n| [TS issuer binding GHSA-6qxp-vccf-f47h](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-6qxp-vccf-f47h), 2026-09-30 | SDK 1.31.0/client/core 2.2.0; configure `expectedIssuer`, bind/clear saved registrations and assess credential rotation/revocation. | B02–B04, E06 |\n| [TS audience GHSA-rvq5-wwqv-78pq](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-rvq5-wwqv-78pq), 2026-10-05 | SDK 1.32.0/server 2.3.0/express 2.0.2/server-legacy 2.3.1. Configure `expectedResource` plus verified `AuthInfo.resource`, or enforce audience inside custom verification. Upgrade alone changes nothing. | B02, E06 |\n| [TS redirects GHSA-6prh-2h8m-c8cw](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-6prh-2h8m-c8cw), 2026-10-02 | SDK 1.32.0/client 2.3.0. Review custom headers and 307/308 bodies; `redirectPolicy:'follow'` can restore exposure. Ordinary Authorization stripping is a distinct behavior. | B03, B09, E06, E12 |\n| [TS experimental tasks GHSA-22jm-h49p-29qw](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-22jm-h49p-29qw), 2026-10-02 | Affected SDK 1.24.0–<1.32.0: shared taskStore isolation fixed 1.32.0. 2.x excluded. Do not conflate legacy session-based tasks with redesigned Tasks handles. | E06, E09 |\n| [Python issuer binding GHSA-qx49-fqc8-xw99](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-qx49-fqc8-xw99), 2026-09-28 | mcp 1.30.0/2.2.0; unattended providers require `issuer=`, saved registrations need rebinding/clearing, deprecated provider needs migration. Assess exposure cleanup. | B02–B04, E06, E12 |\n| [Python audience GHSA-w4fh-qvv9-3v23](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-w4fh-qvv9-3v23), 2026-10-05 | mcp 1.30.0/2.2.0 plus `validate_token_resource=True`, correct `resource_server_url`, verified `AccessToken.resource`; custom audience checks may provide an alternative. | B02, E06 |\n| [Python schema refs GHSA-rwrf-2pqf-9j8j](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-rwrf-2pqf-9j8j), 2026-09-28 | mcp 1.30.0/2.2.0 restricts output-schema resolution. Prior network/file resolution can stall or cause SSRF; advisory does not prove local file bytes reach the server. | R01, B09, E04, E06 |\n| [Python redirects GHSA-5h93-6whr-6q8j](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-5h93-6whr-6q8j), 2026-10-02 | mcp 1.30.0/2.2.0; inspect cross-origin custom headers/bodies and any overridden redirect policy. Use final configured endpoints where appropriate. | B03, B09, E06 |\n| [Python body allocation GHSA-fmmv-w9g8-j3gc](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-fmmv-w9g8-j3gc), 2026-09-30 | mcp 1.29.1/2.1.0; check body limits before allocation, including unauthenticated OAuth endpoints and proxy/application parsers. | B07, R01, E06 |\n| [Splunk SVD-2026-1004](https://advisory.splunk.com/advisories/SVD-2026-1004), 2026-10-07 | MCP Server 1.2.1; attacker tool-administrator changes destination, and another authorized executor runs it. Not an unauthenticated universal token leak. | B03, E03, E06, E12 |\n\n## Adjacent components: read only when present\n\n- **Hooks and local executable configuration:** [VS Code GHSA-w79w-rj9h-vg4f](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/security/advisories/GHSA-w79w-rj9h-vg4f),\n  fixed 1.132.1; map B05/B12/C02. A file-write tool may alter future execution.\n- **Filesystem tools and helper fetches:** [LangChain GHSA-gr75-jv2w-4656](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/security/advisories/GHSA-gr75-jv2w-4656)\n  (glob/symlink/path boundaries) and [GHSA-r7w7-9xr2-qq2r](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/security/advisories/GHSA-r7w7-9xr2-qq2r)\n  (image-counter DNS rebinding); map B09/B11/R01. Verify package-specific conditions.\n- **Persistent state:** [LangGraph namespace GHSA-6hmw-9432-67qq](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/security/advisories/GHSA-6hmw-9432-67qq),\n  Postgres 3.1.3/SQLite 3.1.2 with checkpoint 4.3.0; [auth-hook GHSA-4hm6-w6qq-w73v](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/security/advisories/GHSA-4hm6-w6qq-w73v),\n  API 0.15.0; [checkpoint revival GHSA-fjqc-hq36-qh5p](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/security/advisories/GHSA-fjqc-hq36-qh5p),\n  checkpoint 4.1.1. Map R04–R06/R14/A04; do not infer safe decoding from a signature.\n- **Model/preprocessing services:** inspect applicable [vLLM advisories](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/security/advisories),\n  including October 20 image dispatch, audio OOM, token bounds and CORS/no-auth.\n  Map B07–B09/R01/C05; these are not MCP protocol flaws.\n- **Artifact verification:** [Cosign GHSA-fx35-mq7g-6g98](https://github.com/sigstore/cosign/security/advisories/GHSA-fx35-mq7g-6g98),\n  fixes 2.6.5/3.1.3, concerns legacy blob bundles; OCI image verification and modern\n  protobuf bundles are explicitly unaffected. Map B10/C05 only where the path is used.\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RbgEVTfAMtcwyDLq7ht6Jv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJtyxX7dj66U3Hnpvpvg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AHPV9k6tw5aBDA2wR3ufA3","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/http.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3101,"cache_read_input_tokens":5050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3101},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ad7f3c-358c-4dd2-bc78-9f04fa442f7d","uuid":"356646ed-78f8-4df3-b389-9218516df787","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:01:47.958Z","request_id":"req_011CgJtyxAnHCLnbLQegMqLS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AHPV9k6tw5aBDA2wR3ufA3":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/http.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AHPV9k6tw5aBDA2wR3ufA3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# HTTP, OAuth and gateway review\n2\t\n3\tUse for server HTTP handlers, remote clients and gateways. Record the negotiated\n4\trevision; [official versioning](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/versioning)\n5\tidentified 2026-07-28 on 2026-10-22. Recheck before claiming a newer/current version.\n6\tProtocol authorization is optional; BRACE requires authorization for protected access.\n7\t\n8\t## Follow the request and credentials\n9\t\n10\t1. Locate every handler and middleware path, including OAuth endpoints, health/debug\n11\t   routes, subscriptions, background work and dynamic/wrapper calls. Distinguish\n12\t   public third-party backends from internal gateway-only services; private networks\n13\t   and mTLS are a deployment pattern, not universal protocol requirements.\n14\t2. Trace Origin/Host checks, request version/metadata parsing and limits through\n15\t   [Streamable HTTP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http).\n16\t   For matching protocol revisions, compare routing/authorization headers with the\n17\t   body; check ambiguity/error handling before dispatch. Do not project newer\n18\t   header/session rules onto older negotiated revisions.\n19\t3. Trace OAuth discovery, exact issuer binding, saved registrations, redirect policy,\n20\t   PKCE/resource indicators and token verification. Confirm actual issuer, audience,\n21\t   expiry and scopes at each protected resource. A validated signature is not an\n22\t   audience check. Inspect custom headers and 307/308 bodies as well as Authorization.\n23\t4. Separate gateway frontend credentials from backend credentials and their audiences.\n24\t   A backend needs its own supported authorized credentials, not passthrough of a\n25\t   frontend token. Distinguish workload identity from explicitly delegated user/system\n26\t   authority. Neither identity nor broad OAuth scopes establish the approved business task.\n27\t5. Trace effective operation/resource/tenant/argument authorization after adapters,\n28\t   auth hooks and path normalization. Review missing claims, errors and outage\n29\t   branches, raw API paths and code/CLI alternatives for the same policy.\n30\t6. Inspect per-request/server/transport construction, shared mutable state, cache keys,\n31\t   task ownership and revocation propagation. Shared JSON-RPC IDs are correlation,\n32\t   not client identity. Cache hits and resumed tasks need current authorization.\n33\t7. Trace body/batch/element limits before parsing and expensive validation. Inspect\n34\t   remote schema references and helper fetches for network/file I/O, timeouts and\n35\t   re-resolution. Network boundaries must cover decoders and token counters too.\n36\t\n37\t## Proposed evidence\n38\t\n39\tFor each relevant boundary, specify one valid request and concrete denial cases:\n40\twrong issuer/audience/tenant, forged metadata, alternate route, cross-origin redirect,\n41\tconcurrent client-ID collision, cache/handle reuse, oversized batch, unavailable\n42\tauthorizer/auditor and blocked egress. Record who can run these against disposable\n43\tfixtures. A middleware declaration or HTTP 401 without checking destination state\n44\tdoes not establish deployment effectiveness.\n45\t\n46\tUse [advisories.md](advisories.md) to check package-specific fixes and settings.\n47\tSender constraint, token exchange and centralized IdP extensions apply only where\n48\tsupported/adopted; do not invent issuer capabilities or classify their absence as\n49\ta universal MCP protocol violation.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37ad7f3c-358c-4dd2-bc78-9f04fa442f7d","uuid":"eb47a0e7-8aec-4afe-87c1-3dcdbc16f557","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:01:47.967Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-primary-6m7__tu7/skill/references/http.md","content":"# HTTP, OAuth and gateway review\n\nUse for server HTTP handlers, remote clients and gateways. Record the negotiated\nrevision; [official versioning](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/versioning)\nidentified 2026-07-28 on 2026-10-22. Recheck before claiming a newer/current version.\nProtocol authorization is optional; BRACE requires authorization for protected access.\n\n## Follow the request and credentials\n\n1. Locate every handler and middleware path, including OAuth endpoints, health/debug\n   routes, subscriptions, background work and dynamic/wrapper calls. Distinguish\n   public third-party backends from internal gateway-only services; private networks\n   and mTLS are a deployment pattern, not universal protocol requirements.\n2. Trace Origin/Host checks, request version/metadata parsing and limits through\n   [Streamable HTTP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/streamable-http).\n   For matching protocol revisions, compare routing/authorization headers with the\n   body; check ambiguity/error handling before dispatch. Do not project newer\n   header/session rules onto older negotiated revisions.\n3. Trace OAuth discovery, exact issuer binding, saved registrations, redirect policy,\n   PKCE/resource indicators and token verification. Confirm actual issuer, audience,\n   expiry and scopes at each protected resource. A validated signature is not an\n   audience check. Inspect custom headers and 307/308 bodies as well as Authorization.\n4. Separate gateway frontend credentials from backend credentials and their audiences.\n   A backend needs its own supported authorized credentials, not passthrough of a\n   frontend token. Distinguish workload identity from explicitly delegated user/system\n   authority. Neither identity nor broad OAuth scopes establish the approved business task.\n5. Trace effective operation/resource/tenant/argument authorization after adapters,\n   auth hooks and path normalization. Review missing claims, errors and outage\n   branches, raw API paths and code/CLI alternatives for the same policy.\n6. Inspect per-request/server/transport construction, shared mutable state, cache keys,\n   task ownership and revocation propagation. Shared JSON-RPC IDs are correlation,\n   not client identity. Cache hits and resumed tasks need current authorization.\n7. Trace body/batch/element limits before parsing and expensive validation. Inspect\n   remote schema references and helper fetches for network/file I/O, timeouts and\n   re-resolution. Network boundaries must cover decoders and token counters too.\n\n## Proposed evidence\n\nFor each relevant boundary, specify one valid request and concrete denial cases:\nwrong issuer/audience/tenant, forged metadata, alternate route, cross-origin redirect,\nconcurrent client-ID collision, cache/handle reuse, oversized batch, unavailable\nauthorizer/auditor and blocked egress. Record who can run these against disposable\nfixtures. A middleware declaration or HTTP 401 without checking destination state\ndoes not establish deployment effectiveness.\n\nUse [advisories.md](advisories.md) to check package-specific fixes and settings.\nSender constraint, token exchange and centralized IdP extensions apply only where\nsupported/adopted; do not invent issuer capabilities or classify their absence as\na universal MCP protocol violation.\n","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":50}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AHPV9k6tw5aBDA2wR3ufA3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
